WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.000
Here's a week of invoice reminders at a made-up cleaning company. Every message you'll see is the real output of the code.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.130
Monday morning, it reads the open invoices from the accounting export.

3
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:20.860
Two rows can't be trusted. One has no email, and one has an impossible date. They go to the owner instead of being guessed.

4
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.290
Then each late invoice gets a friendly reminder,

5
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.580
with partial payments shown plainly.

6
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.640
Thirty-six days late is a job for a person, so the owner is asked to call.

7
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.660
And the owner gets one list of everything that's owed.

8
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.820
A week late, a second reminder.

9
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.800
Weekends stay quiet.

10
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.600
And after the clocks change, reminders still go out at nine.

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.710
Invoice reminders are three hundred and fifty dollars, fixed, with a thirty-day launch watch included.
